# nr-tui-switch: the `mixdog` binary runs the terminal interface and the --plain REPL.
# Files: crates/mixdog-entry/{Cargo.toml, src/interactive.rs, tests/node_free.rs, tests/pty_twin.rs, tests/support/*}.
# Nothing here was compiled (no cargo in this task). The crate is not a workspace member until nr-tui-entry-argv.wire section 1 is applied;
# mixdog-tui and mixdog-repl are (their own wires: nr-tui-app-run, nr-tui-repl).

## 1. native/core/Cargo.lock
Package `mixdog-entry`: `dependencies` gain (alphabetical, merged into the list nr-tui-entry-argv.wire section 3 describes):
 "mixdog-core-session", "mixdog-fsio", "mixdog-repl", "mixdog-tui", "mixdog-tui-style", "mixdog-view-model"
and the dev-dependencies add "mixdog-term" and "portable-pty". All are workspace crates or crates already in the lock (portable-pty is
mixdog-term's and mixdog-tui's dev-dependency). No package is added to the lock.
No workspace Cargo.toml change: every one of them is already a [workspace.dependencies] entry (mixdog-tui, mixdog-repl, mixdog-tui-style,
mixdog-view-model, mixdog-core-session, mixdog-fsio, mixdog-term, portable-pty).

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml
`cargo hakari generate` after the members of nr-tui-entry-argv.wire section 1 and nr-tui-repl.wire section 1 are in.
D:\mixdog-build\tools\unify-test-features.py for mixdog-entry (its tests now build mixdog-term and portable-pty, which carry no test-only feature).

## 3. compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING
Nothing: the crate registers no protocol method.

## 4. What interactive.rs does (so the wiring can check it)
- dispatch.rs (nr-tui-entry-argv, unchanged here) brackets every non-exec run with the lifecycle ledger (begin/finish_process_lifecycle,
  record_catchable_fatal), performs the pending staged swap and re-runs itself with MIXDOG_SWAP_REEXEC=1 returning the child's code, and
  registers the live session; interactive.rs only maps options and calls the run.
- `Mode::Tui` calls `mixdog_tui::run::run_tui(TuiOptions { provider, model, effort, fast, web_search, tool_mode: "full"|"readonly",
  remote, force_onboarding, worktree: {mode:"worktree",name}|{mode:"branch"}|none, cwd: None, resume: None })`.
- `Mode::Plain` calls `mixdog_repl::run(ReplOptions { provider, model, tool_mode, cwd: None }, Arc<StatuslineRenderer>)`.
- The exit code is read back from the `ExitCode` run_tui / run return, by its Debug text (the type has no accessor). One-line follow-up for
  the owners of mixdog-tui/src/run.rs and mixdog-repl/src/lib.rs: expose the `i32` their `ExitCode` is made from (`run_tui_code`,
  `run_code`), then delete `exit_code_of` in interactive.rs.

## 5. Packaging (decision D7: the binary beside `mixdogd`; the owner's installer decides PATH)
- package.json: `bin.mixdog` stops pointing at src/cli.mjs. With the native distribution it names the shim the installer puts beside
  `mixdogd` (or `bin` is removed when the npm package is retired). Remove the script `build:tui` and the `build:tui` step of `prepack`
  (`"prepack": "npm run build:shipped-history"`), and the script `bench:tui-load`.
- Installer / release scripts (the packaging task of the wave that publishes the CLI): place `mixdog` (`mixdog.exe`) in the same folder as
  `mixdogd` (ensure_core's `core_binary` looks beside the running executable), publish `mixdog-cli-manifest.json` as nr-tui-launch-update.wire
  section 4 says, and add the folder to PATH as the owner decides.
- Run once the pieces above exist: `cargo test --offline -p mixdog-entry`, `... --test node_free`, `... --test pty_twin -- --ignored`
  (a machine with node and C:/Project/mixdog; MIXDOGD_BIN = a mixdogd built with the test-support feature of mixdog-ai, for the pty runs).

## 6. Deletion list (task nr-tui-delete, wave 10: only after node_free and pty_twin are green and the import-closure check passes)
The Node TUI is not kept behind any switch. The list is plan-tui.json `deletions` as it stands: src/cli.mjs, src/app.mjs, src/help.mjs,
src/headless-command.mjs (+ test); src/repl.mjs and src/repl/**; src/tui/** except the files the Electron renderer imports (decision D9);
src/ui/{ansi,markdown,session-stats,statusline,statusline-agents,stream-finalize,tool-card}.mjs and their tests; src/vendor/statusline/**
when no daemon importer remains; src/standalone/session-client.mjs and session-client/**, folder-dialog.mjs; src/runtime/shared/
{staged-update,process-lifecycle,staged-child-result}.mjs when no importer remains; scripts/build-tui.mjs, tui-frame-harness.mjs,
tui-transcript-jitter-harness-entry.jsx, tui-perf-run.ps1, tui-runtime-load-bench.mjs, markdown-surface-test.mjs; the package.json
dependencies only that code used (ink, react (root), marked, cli-highlight, string-width, strip-ansi, wrap-ansi, chalk, diff) after the check.

## 7. Not done by this task (reported in its result)
The statusline of `--plain` is built from a StatusHost that has no model catalog, plan-usage cache or session runtimes (they are the core's,
not this process's): the model-window, quota and sub-agent segments are what the files of the data folder give, no more. The footer of the
terminal interface itself is not painted by mixdog-tui's run loop yet (render.rs passes footer ""), which is nr-tui-app-run's.
